**Authentication:**
- Uses **Supabase** for user identity management
- Token stored in system keychain (macOS/Windows)
- Token sent in HTTP `Authorization: Bearer <token>` header
- Proxy validates token and forwards request to Anthropic API

---

### 5. OVERALL CONTROL FLOW: USER MESSAGE → AGENT ACTIONS

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ USER SENDS MESSAGE (agent_frame.cpp:1854-1880)                  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  1. User types message in chat UI and presses Send              │
│  2. OnChatInputSubmitted() → m_chatController->SendMessage()    │
│  3. Message added to m_chatHistory with role:"user"             │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ LLM REQUEST (chat_controller.cpp:SendMessage)                   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  4. Gather tools available for current editor state:            │
│     - If schematic open: include SCHEMATIC group tools          │
│     - If PCB open: include PCB group tools                      │
│     - Always include GENERAL group tools                        │
│                                                                  │
│  5. Build request:                                              │
│     - Model: "claude-opus-4-7" (default)                        │
│     - System prompt: core.md + agent.md + (plan.md if PLAN)    │
│     - Messages: full chat history                               │
│     - Tools: available tool schemas with input_schema           │
│                                                                  │
│  6. Call m_llmClient->AskStreamWithToolsAsync( messages,        │
│     tools, handler )                                             │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ CURL STREAMING (agent_llm_client.cpp:Entry)                     │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│  7. Background thread created (LLM_REQUEST_THREAD)              │
│  8. POST to https://<ZEO_BASE_URL>/api/llm/messages            │
│     - Header: Authorization: Bearer <Supabase token>           │
│     - Body: { model, messages, stream:true, max_tokens, tools,  │
│              metadata: { agent_mode, system_prompt, ... } }    │
│  9. Proxy validates token, forwards to Anthropic API           │
│ 10. Stream SSE response (Server-Sent Events)                    │
│     - Line 1: event: content_block_start                       │
│     - Line 2: data: {"type":"text",...}                        │
│     - Increment for text content or tool_use.input             │
│     - Line N: event: content_block_stop                        │
│     - Empty line \n\n marks end of event                       │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ PARSE STREAMING CHUNKS (agent_llm_client.cpp:StreamWriteCallback)
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 11. For each \n\n-delimited SSE event:                          │
│     - Extract event type (content_block_start, delta, stop)    │
│     - Extract data (JSON payload)                               │
│     - If type:"tool_use": accumulate id, name, input            │
│     - Post wxThreadEvent (EVT_LLM_STREAM_CHUNK) to main thread │
│                                                                  │
│ 12. EVT_LLM_STREAM_CHUNK carries:                               │
│     LLM_EVENT_TYPE type (TEXT, TOOL_USE, TOOL_USE_DONE, etc.)  │
│     std::string text                                             │
│     std::string tool_use_id, tool_name                          │
│     nlohmann::json tool_input                                   │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ MAIN THREAD RECEIVES CHUNKS (agent_frame.cpp:OnLLMStreamChunk)  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 13. OnLLMStreamChunk( wxThreadEvent ) fires in main thread      │
│ 14. m_chatController->HandleStreamChunk( event )                │
│     - Accumulates text into response                            │
│     - On TOOL_USE events: creates PendingToolCall               │
│     - On TOOL_USE_DONE: emits EVT_CHAT_TOOL_READY               │
│     - On END_TURN: emits EVT_CHAT_TURN_COMPLETE                │
│                                                                  │
│ 15. Render streaming response in UI (HTML)                      │
│     - Text blocks appear immediately                            │
│     - Tool calls show as expandable "Thinking..." → description │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ TOOL EXECUTION (chat_controller.cpp:ExecuteAllTools)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 16. When LLM finishes (no more tools or END_TURN):              │
│     - Transition to EXECUTING_TOOL state                        │
│     - Emit EVT_CHAT_STATE_CHANGED                               │
│     - Batch all pending tool calls                              │
│                                                                  │
│ 17. For each tool call:                                         │
│     a) Classify tool type:                                      │
│        - Frame-managed (open_editor, sch_run_erc): deferred    │
│        - IPC tools (sch_add, pcb_place, etc.): execute parallel│
│        - Direct tools (check_status, screenshot): exec direct  │
│                                                                  │
│     b) IPC Tools → TOOL_REGISTRY::Execute()                     │
│        - Route to appropriate TOOL_HANDLER                      │
│        - For PYTHON_TOOL_HANDLER:                               │
│          * Load Python script from disk                         │
│          * Build IPC command: "run_shell <app> <preamble><script>"
│          * Send to editor via MAIL_AGENT_REQUEST message        │
│          * Editor executes in sandboxed Python environment     │
│          * Editor replies with MAIL_AGENT_RESPONSE              │
│        - Result: JSON output from script                        │
│                                                                  │
│     c) Direct Tools → TOOL_HANDLER::Execute()                   │
│        - CHECK_STATUS_HANDLER: Returns current editor/project   │
│        - SCREENSHOT_HANDLER: Captures and encodes UI            │
│        - FILE_IO_HANDLER: Read/write files                      │
│        - Result: Returned immediately                           │
│                                                                  │
│ 18. Time each tool execution (for analytics)                    │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ TOOL RESULTS ADDED TO HISTORY                                   │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 19. For each completed tool:                                    │
│     m_chatController->HandleToolResult( toolId, result,success) │
│     - Adds to history: { role: "user",                          │
│                          content: [{ type: "tool_result",       │
│                                      tool_use_id: toolId,       │
│                                      content: result }] }       │
│     - Emits EVT_CHAT_TOOL_RESULT (UI updates)                  │
│     - Logs to AGENT_MONITOR_LOG for analytics                  │
│                                                                  │
│ 20. When all tools complete:                                    │
│     - Transition to WAITING_FOR_LLM                             │
│     - Emit EVT_CHAT_STATE_CHANGED                               │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ CONTINUE CHAT (chat_controller.cpp:ContinueChat)                │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 21. LLM request continues with full history:                    │
│     [user msg, assistant (text + tool_use), user (tool_results),
│      <NEW LLM TURN: can call more tools or respond>]           │
│                                                                  │
│ 22. Return to step 11 (parse streaming chunks) for new tools OR │
│     Proceed to step 23 if LLM response complete (no more tools) │
└────────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                 │
                 ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ FINAL RESPONSE (agent_frame.cpp:OnLLMStreamComplete)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ 23. When LLM finishes with no more tool calls:                  │
│     - Background thread posts EVT_LLM_STREAM_COMPLETE          │
│     - OnLLMStreamComplete() clears m_requestInProgress flag    │
│     - Render final response text in chat                        │
│     - Save chat snapshot to database                            │
│     - Transition to READY state                                 │
│     - User can send next message                                │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

